&lt;h2&gt;GAME DESIGN INTERN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Game Design Intern to join the Fortnite Events team and help create memorable large scale multiplayer experiences. You will work with internal and co-dev designers, artists, engineers and producers to prototype, implement and polish gameplay features for upcoming live events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and implement gameplay features for live events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn how to prototype dynamic player experiences in a large scale client-server replicated environment and expand on those ideas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Work within level sequences to help align keyframed event triggers, work with cinematic artists to manage structure and timing, and implement gameplay features into the event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Participate in team playtests, providing and addressing feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Collaborate with others and independently iterate on work based on feedback and evolving needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Clearly communicate updates, progress, and potential risks to relevant stakeholders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Make and update documents for designs, technical adjustments, or reference materials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Practical experience with Unreal Engine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Proficiency with Blueprints and the Gameplay Ability System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Portfolio of playable projects demonstrating experience across the video game production cycle, including student, indie, or freelance work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in Fortnite, particularly live events and ambitious, narrative-driven content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Experience with level design systems such as World Partition and Data Layers, Level Sequencer, and basic multiplayer replication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to independently troubleshoot problems and use available resources to identify solutions to blocking issues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to clearly communicate needs, risks, ideas, scope, and progress to the team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively across disciplines to safely implement content into a project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to debug systems and interactive gameplay issues and develop test plans that support both debugging and QA validation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
