&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ENGINEERING - UNREAL ENGINE&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unreal-powered projects have been on the bleeding edge of real-time entertainment for over 20 years. Our team of engineering experts are always innovating to improve the tools and technology that empower content developers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Principal Al Engineer who builds products that integrate Al into Unreal Engine. You&#39;ll design and ship the full stack of systems that let LLMs act inside the engine (from end to end, not just a single layer), bringing depth in game engine architecture, cloud services, and how LLMs actually work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build LLM-driven agents and tools that operate directly inside Unreal Engine, including engine-side C++/Python tooling and editor scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and extend the cloud-hosted agent harness, services, and database that mediate between LLMs and the engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the full stack (engine tooling, cloud backend, and the web UI used to drive and monitor agents) to ship end-to-end features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and integrate emerging LLM capabilities (tool use, multi-agent orchestration, context management) into Epic&#39;s engine and pipeline tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define technical direction for the reliability, safety, and evaluation of LLM-driven engine automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engine, tools, and backend engineers, and mentor others on both game engine internals and LLM system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming background with hands-on experience in a game engine (Unreal Engine strongly preferred), including engine architecture and tooling/editor scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience building or shipping products powered by LLMs (agents, tool-calling, RAG, prompt/context engineering), or a strong conceptual understanding of how LLMs work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud-native services and infrastructure: web APIs, databases, and service architecture and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent programming skills across C++ (engine-side) and Python and/or a web backend language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the games industry or equivalent, developing interactive entertainment products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work full-stack and reason about tradeoffs across engine code, backend services, and a web front end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a BS/MS in Computer Science or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
