&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;DESIGN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put your design skills to work at a cutting-edge company that challenges the norm. From character and level design to competitive gameplay and system design, help shape the future of interactive entertainment at Epic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate with cross-disciplinary development teams to design, prototype, implement, and ship key features that expand the Fortnite universe. As a Senior Mobile Game Designer, you&#39;ll own features and systems for our mobile players, building new areas of the game and improving existing ones from initial vision through polished player-facing experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Major Features: Drive the design and development of significant mobile features, such as gameplay and progression systems, from concept through launch, establishing a clear vision, documentation, implementation plan, and path to a high-quality player experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Shape the Big-Picture Vision: Contribute to broader product and gameplay decisions by identifying opportunities, evaluating trade-offs, and helping the team prioritize features that deliver meaningful value to our mobile players&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Champion the Mobile Player Experience: Apply a deep understanding of player motivations and behaviors to create compelling goals, gameplay loops, and experiences that keep players engaged over time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Drive Prototyping &amp;amp; Iteration: Lead rapid prototyping and iteration loops, using everything from early design pitches and paper concepts to playable in-engine prototypes to validate ideas and solve complex mobile design problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Raise the Design Bar: Provide thoughtful feedback and design guidance to other team members and evangelize mobile design best practices within the wider Fortnite team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Partner Across Disciplines: Communicate design intent clearly and build alignment across teams while collaborating on developing new features, ensuring the vision, design and player experience are primed for our mobile audience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Leverage Playtests &amp;amp; Data: Regularly participate in playtests and design reviews, synthesizing feedback, player insights, and gameplay data into actionable steps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Implement in Blueprint: Work hands-on in Unreal Engine to prototype and implement designs using Blueprint scripting, partnering closely with engineering, animation, VFX, audio, art, and other disciplines to bring features to life&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;5+ years of professional mobile game design experience, with a track record of designing and shipping high-quality features or systems (such as progression systems, core shooter gameplay, and action game mechanics)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Demonstrated experience independently owning complex features from early concept and prototyping through implementation, iteration, polish, release and live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Deep understanding of mobile-specific design, such as engagement systems, touch controls, screen real estate, session length, and UX/UI conventions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong hands-on experience working in Unreal Engine, including Blueprint scripting and implementing gameplay directly in-engine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Experience designing content, features, or systems for Games-as-a-Service (GaaS), live-service games, or highly active online multiplayer ecosystems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong understanding of multiplayer game design and a passion for Battle Royale and other large-scale multiplayer experiences&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;A strong ability to understand player motivations, behaviors, and different forms of play, and to translate those insights into compelling mobile gameplay experiences&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Proven ability to evaluate ideas, navigate ambiguity, and make thoughtful decisions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
